casey frey's get the f out my way type  way is one of the most artfully produced  videos online today  the video tells the story of a man  rejecting criticism and using dance to  express his true self but within such a  seemingly simple story frey uses  innovative film language and symbolism  to create not only an addictive to watch  viral video but also a cinematic  masterpiece that continues to impact the  dance videos we see today  first we see the main character chop a  piece of wood then the camera pans up to  a medium shot notice how the character  straightens up to full height as the  camera follows him this movement with  the camera adds energy to the shot  and guides our eyesight to his first  shoulder dance move near the top of the  frame  this same camera movement later  visualizes his connection with his good  alter ego  after the good alter ego pulses his  chest we cut to the main character and  both he  and the camera are looking inward but  then they both move outward  showing how the good alter ego's  contagious energy infected him on the  inside from here the camera moves with  full force it travels up his body as his  energy moves from his foot  up to his hips then to his arms and his  good alter ego similarly moves with the  camera as they connect  frey uses matching shots to seamlessly  transition between the two characters as  they move as one and they finally join  forces in the final frame of the video  to add contrast to this connection the  bad alter ego is filmed in a mostly  static frame and the camera doesn't  follow his movements at all  in his last shot he rejects the movement  entirely frank gives his video energy  not just from the camera but from his  cuts like when he cuts to the beat of  the music  he also skips frames to make his  movement appear more snappy or when he  flips off his bad alter ego repeats  frames to add emphasis to his leg and  hand movements  these cuts combined with the camera  movement create a sequence with an  electric hypnotizing energy to really  get a feel for how well he executed this  video  compare it to the countless recreation  videos while many of them are great they  still reveal just how much precision  frey put into the editing and camera  work in the original but get the f  out of my way type way is more than just  a snappy dance video it has its own  story one with a complete hero's journey  the main character has a call to  adventure when starting his dance but he  refuses the call  after getting rejected then he meets a  mentor who helps him cross the threshold  overcome the abyss of rejection and  transform the story's meaning can be  interpreted in many ways  and i'm not the first to acknowledge it  feels like it's about the workers  revolution  it can be read as the story of a working  class man rejecting his manual labor job  and joining a collective in that case  the heartbeat is a symbol of the  awakening of class consciousness in the  worker and the bad alter ego is a symbol  for the ruling class who wants to  maintain the status quo  there's even a prominent sign on the  glass door that slides across the frame  that says this property is under video  surveillance  a message which makes the area feel like  an intrusive work zone but i think a big  reason frey's video has remained so  relevant for so long  is because of its universal message of  rejecting the haters and embracing your  true self  that general appeal may partly explain  why the video became its own meme format  in this meme the bad alter ego can be  any negative force  and the main character is a rejection of  that instruction and phrase video  continues to impact the dance videos we  see  online it's one of the most popular  examples of having the camera follow the  movement of the dancer a technique that  has become a dance video staple  and the storytelling in his dance moves  sets a standard for character-driven  choreography and for anybody who doesn't  appreciate the cinematic artistry of  this video  all i have to say to you is get out my  way  [Music]
 

